    <tags>audio fade pause resume seek wasapi tray windows foss</tags>
    <summary>System tray app that fades audio on pause, resume and seek for all apps.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
Pause Resume Audio Fade for Windows fades the sound of **any application** when you pause, resume or seek
(browsers, video and music players): no more abrupt cut-offs, and a soft fade-in on resume.

It delays the audio by a short lookahead and applies the fade-out retroactively, then plays it on your real output.

## Requirements
- An unused output device to route the original sound to: the free virtual cable [VB-CABLE](https://vb-audio.com/Cable/)
  **or** a spare output device (a second output such as speakers + headphones, or an HDMI monitor).
  A first-run guide in the app explains this and detects it automatically once available.
- No .NET installation needed (self-contained).

## Notes
- The app runs in the system tray (right-click the icon for settings, auto-start and exit).
- It does not access the internet and does not record or store audio.
- The executable is not code-signed, so Windows SmartScreen may warn on first launch ("More info" > "Run anyway").
- Start it from the Start menu ("Pause Resume Audio Fade") or run `PauseResumeAudioFade`.
    ]]></description>
